Here are a couple of concise functional approaches in Python.

Approach 1: using set comparison
- Converts each string to a set of characters (distinct chars) and compares the sets.

def have_same_distinct_chars(s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:
    return set(s1) == set(s2)

Example:
print(have_same_distinct_chars("abc", "cab"))  # True
print(have_same_distinct_chars("aabb", "ab"))  # True
print(have_same_distinct_chars("abc", "abcd")) # False

Approach 2: using set operations explicitly (same result)
def have_same_distinct_chars_alt(s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:
    return (set(s1) - set(s2)) == set() and (set(s2) - set(s1)) == set()

But the first approach is simpler and idiomatic Python.

